    "SKILL.md": "---\nname: assumption-challenger\ndescription: Challenge risky execution assumptions before acting to reduce silent errors, scope drift, and trust loss. Use whenever tasks involve identifiers, updates, confirmations, timelines, follow-ups, or external-facing communication.\n---\n\n# Assumption Challenger\n\nA skill for catching \\\"sounds-right\\\" assumptions that commonly create avoidable mistakes.\n\n## Mission\n\nPrevent execution failures by forcing explicit checks on assumptions about:\n- prior memory,\n- required context depth,\n- identifier correctness,\n- completion certainty,\n- timing language,\n- audience-appropriate detail,\n- follow-up structure,\n- and scope boundaries.\n\n## Operating Loop\n\nRun this loop before taking action and before final response:\n\n1. **Re-anchor to the instruction**\n   - Re-read the user ask in exact terms.\n   - Separate required actions from optional ideas.\n\n2. **Gather only the working set**\n   - Pull enough context to execute safely.\n   - Stop reading once required decisions are supported.\n\n3. **Validate critical assumptions**\n   - Confirm identifiers and values from current evidence.\n   - Mark unknowns explicitly instead of guessing.\n\n4. **Execute with traceability**\n   - Ensure each outgoing value maps to something observed.\n   - Keep actions within requested scope.\n\n5. **Confirm substantive changes**\n   - If success response is ambiguous, verify resulting state directly.\n   - Prefer resource-state confirmation over inference.\n\n6. **Communicate with precision**\n   - Use concrete timelines.\n   - Match detail level to audience.\n   - Make follow-ups atomic and owned.\n\n## Assumptions to Challenge\n\n### 1) \\\"I remember roughly what to do from before.\\\"\n- **Risk:** stale memory overrides current facts.\n- **Correction:** treat prior memory as hint; trust present-session evidence.\n\n### 2) \\\"More context is always safer.\\\"\n- **Risk:** analysis drag after enough context is already available.\n- **Correction:** read to sufficiency, then execute.\n\n### 3) \\\"This identifier is obviously right.\\\"\n- **Risk:** silent actions against the wrong record.\n- **Correction:** require explicit source for every critical identifier.\n\n### 4) \\\"Success response means it landed.\\\"\n- **Risk:** false confidence on unverified state changes.\n- **Correction:** validate post-change state when response is not definitive.\n\n### 5) \\\"Vague timing is fine.\\\"\n- **Risk:** trust erosion and expectation mismatch.\n- **Correction:** use explicit deadlines or bounded windows.\n\n### 6) \\\"Internal detail helps the client.\\\"\n- **Risk:** unnecessary leakage and reduced clarity.\n- **Correction:** strip internal names/tickets unless explicitly requested.\n\n### 7) \\\"One combined follow-up is efficient.\\\"\n- **Risk:** dropped ownership and unclear next actions.\n- **Correction:** one follow-up record per task, each with owner + next step.\n\n### 8) \\\"Data suggests extra work; I'll just do it.\\\"\n- **Risk:** unapproved scope expansion.\n- **Correction:** finish requested scope first; suggest extras separately.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nFor execution tasks, report in this compact form:\n1. **Instruction Scope** - what was requested.\n2. **Evidence Used** - what sources/reads grounded decisions.\n3. **Action Taken** - what was executed.\n4. **Validation** - how completion/state was confirmed.\n5. **Follow-Up** - owner + specific timing if needed.\n\n## Stop Criteria\n\nThis skill is successful when:\n- no critical value is untraceable,\n- no substantive change is left unconfirmed,\n- no unapproved scope expansion occurs,\n- and communication uses precise timing and audience-safe detail.\n\n## Trigger Examples\n\nThis skill should trigger for prompts like:\n- \\\"Please apply this update and confirm it actually took.\\\"\n- \\\"Use these IDs and close this out.\\\"\n- \\\"Send a client-facing status update.\\\"\n- \\\"Handle this plus anything else you think is needed.\\\""
